│ patch.                                                                                                                                         │
│                                                                                                                                                │
│     The fix has two parts:                                                                                                                     │
│     - **Body model creation (`create_body_model`):** the generated body model now gets `ConfigDict(arbitrary_types_allowed=True)`. Before      │
│ this, a route with two body parameters of an arbitrary class failed at startup with "Invalid args for response field".                         │
│     - **Per-field `TypeAdapter` (`ModelField.__post_init__`):** on `PydanticSchemaGenerationError`, it retries with                            │
│ `arbitrary_types_allowed=True`. The retry only happens when the first attempt fails, so ordinary fields are unaffected.                        │
│                                                                                                                                                │
│     Verification was limited. My reproduction script now starts the app and returns the expected 422 for a non-`Foo` body value.               │
│ `tests/test_compat.py` passes (10 passed, 3 skipped). I did not run any test that exercises the response-model path, and I did not check the   │
│ exact upstream behaviour the hidden tests expect.                                                                                              │
